## Context

Agents and humans invoke `erg` directly from skills and Makefiles
(`erg validate`, `erg ready`, `erg close`, and the planned
`erg pick`). That means `erg` must be on PATH in every environment
where agents run: dev machines, CI containers, worktrees. Currently
the binary is committed at `tickets/tools/go/erg` (x86-64 static) and
built into `DEST/tickets/tools/go/erg` by `bin/install.sh`, but
neither location is on PATH.

CLAUDE-PLUGIN.md currently says "no CLI needed" and points to a manual
`go build` note buried under Notes. Both are misleading: agents need
`erg` on PATH to use the plugin's skills.

Two lightweight fixes cover the gap:
1. A Makefile target that puts the binary on PATH — the shared primitive for all
   environments (human dev, CI, devcontainer, agent).
2. A one-liner prerequisite in CLAUDE-PLUGIN.md so agents know exactly what to
   run when `erg` is not found, without needing to reason from scratch.

The SessionStart hook (automatic install on every agent session start) is out of
scope here — it is a follow-up that calls this Makefile target once it exists.

## Actions

1. Add `install-erg-binary` target to `Makefile`:
   - If the committed binary matches the current platform (x86-64 Linux): copy it
     to `~/.local/bin/erg` with `install -m755`.
   - Otherwise: `cd tickets/tools/go && go build -o ~/.local/bin/erg .`
   - Print `erg installed to ~/.local/bin/erg` on success.

2. Update `claude/CLAUDE-PLUGIN.md`:
   - Replace the "no CLI needed" line and buried build note with:
     ```
     ## Prerequisites
     `erg` must be on PATH. If missing: `make install-erg-binary` from the repo root.
     ```

3. Update `bin/install.sh` end-of-run summary to mention `make install-erg-binary`
   alongside the existing success message.

## Test

```bash
# Remove erg from PATH if present
rm -f ~/.local/bin/erg

make install-erg-binary
which erg              # → ~/.local/bin/erg
erg --help             # → exits 0, prints usage

# Idempotent
make install-erg-binary   # → same result, no error
```

## Exit criteria

- `make install-erg-binary` puts a working `erg` binary at `~/.local/bin/erg`
- Works on x86-64 Linux without Go installed (copies committed binary)
- Falls back to `go build` on other platforms if Go is available; fails clearly if not
- `claude/CLAUDE-PLUGIN.md` has a Prerequisites section with the install command
- `bin/install.sh` output mentions `make install-erg-binary`
